<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khakas people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Khakas are a Turkic people of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a> living mainly in the Republic of Khakassia, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minusinsk-basin">Minusinsk Basin</a> on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yenisei-river">Yenisei River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. They are often linked to the medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yenisei-kyrgyz">Yenisei Kyrgyz</a>, whose khaganate ruled the Mongolian steppe in the 9th century. Traditionally herders and farmers, they came under Russian rule in the 17th and 18th centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khakas-people.jpg" alt="Khakas people" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 幻光尘 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khakas_ethnic_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
